# kaniko reads .dockerignore from the build context root, and the backend is its
# own context (Jenkinsfile: helmCharts.kaniko("backend/Dockerfile", "backend",
# ...)). A .dockerignore at the repository root is never read for this build.
#
# Everything listed here is a path the Dockerfile does not COPY — it takes only
# pyproject.toml, poetry.lock, the root-level *.py and app/ — so this file
# cannot change what CI builds. It only stops the dev environment from
# streaming its build and tool output to the builder: the lint and test gates
# leave 13M+ of .mypy_cache behind, which CI never sees because it builds from
# a clean clone.
.git
.venv
**/__pycache__
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.env
.env.*
tests
docs
.claude
logs
tmp
